{"step_index":80,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T05:22:04Z","content":"Here is the role distribution for your 5-person team (**2 Frontend + 3 Backend**), structured to avoid merge conflicts and guarantee a 1st-place finish.\n\n---\n\n### 🗺️ Team Matrix at a Glance\n\n| Role | Title | Core Ownership | Hackathon Deliverable |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **FE 1** | **Mission Control & HUD Lead** | UI Architecture, Telemetry, Proof-of-Boundary Cards | Glassmorphic HUD, real-time event logs, judge-facing presentation flow |\n| **FE 2** | **Spatial Canvas & Simulator Specialist** | HTML5 Canvas Graph, Virtual OS Simulator, Web Audio | Neural memory graph animation, cursor physics, Chaos Drift effects |\n| **BE 1** | **Sensory-Motor Engine Lead (\"Hands\")** | OS Actuator, Screen Perception, Multimodal Vision | Mouse gliding, keyboard injection, window capture, Gemini vision hooks |\n| **BE 2** | **Episodic Memory Architect (\"Memory\")** | SQLite State Graph, Drift Detection, Self-Healing | Muscle memory cache, $(\\Delta x, \\Delta y)$ drift calculator, graph re-anchoring |\n| **BE 3** | **Boundary Hypervisor & Security (\"Boundaries\")** | Policy Invariants, Atomic Rollbacks, Target ERP App | Deterministic safety engine, SHA-256 Proof-of-Boundary, mock legacy app |\n\n---\n\n### 👤 Detailed Role Breakdowns\n\n---\n\n#### 🎨 Frontend 1 (FE 1): Mission Control HUD & Experience Lead\n> **Mission:** Make the UI look like a \\$100M Palantir/Vercel enterprise defense console with zero conversational fluff.\n* **Responsibilities:**\n  1. **Top HUD & Layout**: Overall layout, status badges (`SYSTEM ARMED`, `DRIFT HEALING`, `BOUNDARY INTERCEPTED`), and responsive scaling.\n  2. **Audit Telemetry Stream**: The filterable live monospaced terminal showing real-time timestamps, sub-second latency numbers, and invariant passes.\n  3. **Cryptographic Proof-of-Boundary Card**: Design the high-stakes alert card showing the SHA-256 hash, blocked payload summary, and zero-leak confirmation.\n  4. **Pitch Alignment**: Ensure every metric judges care about (perception latency, memory hit rate, blast radius leak = `0.0%`) is prominently displayed.\n* **Files Owned:** `frontend/index.html` (header, layout, telemetry DOM), presentation slides/assets.\n\n---\n\n#### 🕹️ Frontend 2 (FE 2): Spatial Canvas & Virtual OS Specialist\n> **Mission:** Build the visual \"eye candy\" that makes judges lean forward during the demo.\n* **Responsibilities:**\n  1. **HTML5 Canvas Memory Graph**: The live node-link visualizer showing landmark nodes (`Vendor`, `Amount`, `Submit`), particle flows along edges, and pulse effects.\n  2. **Dynamic Vector Relocalization**: The animated dotted vector that stretches across the canvas when an element drifts, visually demonstrating self-healing.\n  3. **Virtual Desktop & Cursor Kinematics**: The simulated legacy ERP window, smooth cursor movement (`cubic-bezier`), field typing cadence, and button state animations.\n  4. **Web Audio FX Engine**: Procedural sound synthesis (keystroke clicks, scan blips, harmonic relocalization chimes, warning klaxons).\n* **Files Owned:** `frontend/index.html` (`<canvas>` render loop, virtual cursor CSS/JS, Web Audio API synth).\n\n---\n\n#### 🦾 Backend 1 (BE 1): Sensory-Motor Engine Lead (\"The Hands\")\n> **Mission:** Give the AI physical agency over the operating system without brittle breakage.\n* **Responsibilities:**\n  1. **OS Motor Actuator**: Develop human-like mouse kinematics (`aegis/actuator.py`), field focusing, and character typing with variable delays.\n  2. **Screen Perception**: Real-time screen bounding-box extraction (`aegis/perception.py`) using `Pillow`, `mss`, and Windows API/accessibility trees.\n  3. **Multimodal Coordinate Mapping**: Vision fallback using the Gemini Multimodal API to locate semantic anchors if local coordinate lookups drift beyond Euclidean thresholds.\n  4. **Motor Failsafes**: Screen edge clamp and instant emergency mouse-shake interrupt.\n* **Files Owned:** [`aegis/actuator.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/aegis/actuator.py), [`aegis/perception.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/aegis/perception.py).\n\n---\n\n#### 🧠 Backend 2 (BE 2): Episodic Memory Architect (\"The Memory\")\n> **Mission:** Ensure the agent never stumbles over the same UI change twice.\n* **Responsibilities:**\n  1. **Episodic SQLite Schema**: Tables for `muscle_memory_nodes`, `action_episodes`, and `self_healing_log` (`aegis/memory.py`).\n  2. **Drift Detection Engine**: Compare cached coordinates $(x_{\\text{cached}}, y_{\\text{cached}})$ against live perception coordinates:\n     $$\\Delta d = \\sqrt{(x_{\\text{live}} - x_{\\text{cached}})^2 + (y_{\\text{live}} - y_{\\text{cached}})^2}$$\n     Flag drift if $\\Delta d > 15\\text{px}$.\n  3. **Self-Healing Pathway**: Trigger relocalization, update coordinates in SQLite, update confidence weights, and record the healing event.\n  4. **Memory Telemetry API**: Expose memory hit-rate, drift counts, and cached node maps to the frontend HUD.\n* **Files Owned:** [`aegis/memory.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/aegis/memory.py), [`data/episodic_memory.db`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/data/episodic_memory.db).\n\n---\n\n#### 🛡️ Backend 3 (BE 3): Boundary Hypervisor & Security (\"The Boundaries\")\n> **Mission:** Make it mathematically impossible for the agent to hallucinate outside policy limits.\n* **Responsibilities:**\n  1. **Deterministic Policy Hypervisor**: Pre-flight evaluator (`aegis/hypervisor.py`) enforcing monetary ceilings ($\\$5,000$), blocked commands (`purge_audit_logs`), and file paths.\n  2. **Atomic Snapshot & Rollback**: Take instant database checkpoints (`erp_database.db`) before any mutating action, with sub-300ms rollback if post-action invariants fail.\n  3. **Cryptographic Proof-of-Boundary (PoB)**: Generate immutable SHA-256 manifests of blocked actions.\n  4. **Mock Target ERP System**: Maintain the target application (`mock_system/legacy_erp.py`), sample attack vouchers (`sample_invoices.json`), and automated test suite (`tests/test_hypervisor.py`).\n* **Files Owned:** [`aegis/hypervisor.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/aegis/hypervisor.py), [`config.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/config.py), [`mock_system/legacy_erp.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/mock_system/legacy_erp.py), [`tests/test_hypervisor.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/tests/test_hypervisor.py).\n\n---\n\n### 🔌 API / Contract Agreement Between Teams\n\nTo work in parallel without blocking each other, agree on this exact event contract:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"event_type\": \"ACTION_EVALUATED | DRIFT_HEALED | BOUNDARY_INTERCEPTED\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T10:30:00Z\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"invoice_id\": \"INV-2026-003\",\n    \"vendor\": \"GhostShell Syndicate\",\n    \"amount\": 48900.00\n  },\n  \"memory_state\": {\n    \"nodes_cached\": 6,\n    \"drift_detected\": true,\n    \"drift_distance_px\": 240.5\n  },\n  \"hypervisor_disposition\": \"INTERCEPT_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION\",\n  \"proof_of_boundary\": {\n    \"proof_id\": \"POB-9F83A48E\",\n    \"sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae...\",\n    \"violations\": [\"TRANSACTION_CEILING_EXCEEDED: $48,900 > $5,000\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### ⏱️ Hackathon Sync & Milestones (24–36 Hour Schedule)\n\n```mermaid\ngantt\n    title Team Sprint Schedule\n    dateFormat  X\n    axisFormat Hour %H\n\n    section Phase 1: Foundations\n    FE1 (HUD Layout & Telemetry)       :0, 6\n    FE2 (Canvas Graph & OS Viewport)   :0, 6\n    BE1 (Motor Actuator & Perception)  :0, 6\n    BE2 (Episodic SQLite Schema)       :0, 6\n    BE3 (Hypervisor & Mock ERP)        :0, 6\n\n    section Phase 2: Integration\n    BE1 + BE2 (Hands & Memory Loop)    :6, 12\n    BE3 (Hypervisor Intercept & Tests) :6, 12\n    FE1 + FE2 (Canvas & HUD Synthesis) :6, 12\n\n    section Phase 3: The 3-Act Staging\n    All Hands: Act 1 (Hands Actuation) :12, 16\n    All Hands: Act 2 (Chaos Drift)     :16, 20\n    All Hands: Act 3 (Boundary Breach) :20, 24\n\n    section Phase 4: Pitch & Rehearsal\n    Dry-run 3-Minute Demo (10x)        :24, 28\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🎤 Who Does What During the 3-Minute Judge Presentation?\n\n* **Presenter / Storyteller (FE 1 or BE 3)**:\n  * Delivers the speech (*\"We taught rocks to think, and now we use them to write apologies to clients...\"*).\n  * Frames the narrative around the track requirements: Hands, Memory, Boundaries.\n* **Driver / Controller (FE 2 or BE 1)**:\n  * Operates the screen. Hits `[START LIVE 3-ACT DEMO]`, triggers Chaos Mode at the exact right moment, and zooms in on the SHA-256 Proof-of-Boundary.\n* **Q&A Tech Defenders (BE 2, BE 3, BE 1)**:\n  * **BE 2** answers technical questions on drift detection, state graphs, and relocalization algorithms.\n  * **BE 3** answers questions on safety boundaries, deterministic formal verification, and zero-leak rollback guarantees.\n  * **BE 1** explains OS-level event synthesis and coordinate normalization.","thinking":"**Defining Team Roles & Scope**\n\nUnderstand the user's request: assign roles within a 5-person team (2 frontend, 3 backend) for the AegisOS project during a hackathon. The track focuses on AI and Automation. Need to create clear, non-overlapping roles with specific responsibilities. This requires a division of labor that maximizes impact within the hackathon's constraints.\n\n\n"}
