{"step_index":82,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T05:51:41Z","content":"Welcome to the cockpit, **FE 1**! 🚀\n\nAs **Mission Control & HUD Lead**, you own the **first impression and presentation interface** that the judges will be staring at. Your job is to make sure the judges instantly understand:\n1. **There is NO chat window** (Zero-Chat architecture).\n2. **The system state is obvious at a glance** (Safe $\\to$ Drift Healing $\\to$ Boundary Intercepted).\n3. **The Proof-of-Boundary looks like an enterprise-grade cryptographic defense console.**\n\nHere is your exact step-by-step game plan to proceed right now:\n\n---\n\n### ⏱️ Phase 1: Immediate Setup (Next 10 Minutes)\n\n1. **Open and Inspect Your Canvas**:\n   Open the current frontend in your browser:\n   ```powershell\n   start C:\\Users\\Piyush\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\aegis_os\\frontend\\index.html\n   ```\n2. **Run the Demo**:\n   Click **`[RUN 3-ACT DEMO]`** in the top right. Watch the full sequence (Act 1 $\\to$ Act 2 $\\to$ Act 3) to see the baseline you are expanding.\n3. **Understand Your Territory in [`frontend/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/frontend/index.html)**:\n   * **Header & Status Badges**: Lines 60–100 (`#system-status-badge`, navigation).\n   * **Right Column (Boundary Hypervisor & Proof-of-Boundary)**: Lines 275–350 (`#hypervisor-card`, `#pob-card`).\n   * **Telemetry Stream**: Lines 330–370 (`#telemetry-log`, `addLog()`).\n   * **Leave to FE 2**: The `<canvas id=\"memory-canvas\">` and the virtual cursor inside `#desktop-viewport`.\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ Phase 2: High-Impact Upgrades for FE 1 (Hours 1–3)\n\nHere are 3 key features you should implement to take the HUD from great to contest-winning:\n\n---\n\n#### 1. Add Telemetry Filter Chips (Showcase Subsystem Independence)\nJudges love seeing modular architecture. Give them filter tabs on the telemetry log so they can view:\n- `[ALL]` (Everything)\n- `[MOTOR]` (The \"Hands\" actuation events)\n- `[MEMORY]` (Episodic graph & drift healing events)\n- `[HYPERVISOR]` (Boundary contracts & policy passes)\n\n**How to add it to your log section:**\n```html\n<!-- Place above #telemetry-log in the right column -->\n<div class=\"flex items-center space-x-1.5 mb-2 font-mono text-[10px]\">\n  <button onclick=\"filterLogs('all')\" class=\"px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-800 text-cyan-300 border border-cyan-700/50\">ALL</button>\n  <button onclick=\"filterLogs('motor')\" class=\"px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-900 text-slate-400 hover:text-white\">MOTOR</button>\n  <button onclick=\"filterLogs('memory')\" class=\"px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-900 text-slate-400 hover:text-white\">MEMORY</button>\n  <button onclick=\"filterLogs('hypervisor')\" class=\"px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-slate-900 text-slate-400 hover:text-white\">HYPERVISOR</button>\n</div>\n```\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Interactive Cryptographic Proof-of-Boundary Modal\nWhen Act III hits and the \\$48,900 transaction is intercepted, don't just show a small card. Make the Proof-of-Boundary card **clickable** to open a high-tech inspection modal!\n\n**What the modal should show:**\n* **SHA-256 Digest**: `POB-9f83a48e718b2c40c8f1e582c0bdfa35...`\n* **Invariant Contract**: `Rule 01: Max Transaction <= $5,000.00`\n* **Payload Difference**: Requested `+$43,900.00` over permissible threshold.\n* **Pre-Action Snapshot**: State Hash verified identical. Zero data corruption.\n* **A Button**: `[DOWNLOAD AUDIT MANIFEST JSON]` (Judges *love* exportable audit trails).\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Live Presenter Stage Checklist (The \"Pitch Co-Pilot\")\nAdd an expandable floating widget at the bottom of the HUD that tells the team exactly which Act is running and the core talking point for the judges:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"fixed bottom-12 left-6 z-40 bg-slate-900/90 border border-slate-700 backdrop-blur rounded-lg p-3 text-xs font-mono shadow-2xl\">\n  <div class=\"text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase font-bold mb-1\">Judge Presentation Tracker:</div>\n  <div id=\"stage-act-1\" class=\"text-slate-500\">• Act 1: The Hands (Zero-Chat Motor Actuation)</div>\n  <div id=\"stage-act-2\" class=\"text-slate-500\">• Act 2: Memory (Visual Drift Relocalization)</div>\n  <div id=\"stage-act-3\" class=\"text-slate-500\">• Act 3: Boundaries (Deterministic Intercept)</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🤝 How to Sync with Your Teammates\n\n1. **Syncing with FE 2**:\n   * Agree that FE 2 only edits the `<canvas>` animation loop and the `#desktop-viewport` container.\n   * You own the global state object and buttons (`runFullDemo()`, `resetSystem()`).\n   * When FE 2's canvas detects drift, they just call your `addLog(\"DRIFT DETECTED: ...\", \"warn\")`.\n\n2. **Syncing with Backend (BE 1, BE 2, BE 3)**:\n   * Tell BE 3 to provide you with the exact JSON output from [`hypervisor.py`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/aegis/hypervisor.py) so your Proof-of-Boundary modal renders real backend data.\n   * Tell BE 2 to provide the SQLite query results so you can display the \"Total Drifts Healed\" counter accurately.\n\n---\n\n### ⚡ Ready to Code?\nWould you like me to inject the **Telemetry Filter Chips** and the **Interactive Proof-of-Boundary Inspection Modal** into [`frontend/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/frontend/index.html) for you right now, so you can test it live in your browser?","thinking":"**Defining FE1 Responsibilities**\n\nFE1's responsibilities involve the mission control and HUD. This includes the top HUD and layout adhering to a specific aesthetic and incorporating system state badges and branding. Also, it entails a live telemetry and audit stream with specific data filters and timestamps, and cryptographic features.\n\n\n**Prioritizing FE1's Immediate Actions**\n\nIdentify critical areas for initial testing: demo control integration, step-by-step debugger, and stage reset capabilities. Enhance the HUD with an interactive PoB modal, telemetry filter chips, and a live system telemetry bar to elevate the user experience. Integrate a presentation HUD overlay, optimizing for presenter guidance and seamless demo flow.\n\n\n"}
